  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/6a81a657-4b2b-4d70-8f73-ea27f4f9b8bb-1.PNG\"/>\r\n\r\nEquation of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\nLet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> be the mid point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>, so its <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-coordinate of midpoint <math><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>\r\n\r\nHence, coordinates of midpoint <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>\r\n\r\nLet centre of circle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>\r\n\r\nSince, perpendicular dropped from centre upon any chord divides it in two equal parts.\r\n\r\nHence, line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> will be perpendicular to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mi>O</mi></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>R</mi><mi>O</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>\r\n\r\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi> </mi><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>m</mi><mo><</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p>",
